# Reset flathub theming if broken

The cause is usually the global override, so the best option still to reset the file you can find in ./local/share/flatpak/overrides/global 

Commands

First check the status of the file:

flatpak override --user --unset-env=QT_STYLE_OVERRIDE

then the fix:

```
flatpak override --user --unset-env=GTK_THEME
flatpak override --user --unset-env=GTK2_RC_FILES
flatpak override --user --unset-env=QT_STYLE_OVERRIDE
```

then need to do a flatpak update or reboot and it should go back to normality. 

In the folder sometimes you can find other files for some specific apps, delete them and also that apps will restore their normal appearance.
